        "original_id": "cddb9b81-4336-53a7-aa54-243fad8c5a5b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Harrison, Pattie Boyd, Maureen Starkey, Ringo Starr\n- Works: \"Can't Stop Thinking About You\", Extra Texture (Read All About It)\n- Organizations: Apple Records\n- Places: Caxton Hall Register Office, London\n- Topics: marriage, affair, divorce, songwriting, music release\n\nFacts:\n- George Harrison wrote \"Can't Stop Thinking About You\" in December 1973.\n- Maureen Starkey and Ringo Starr married at the Caxton Hall Register Office in London in 1965.\n- George Harrison released \"Can't Stop Thinking About You\" in 1975 on Extra Texture (Read All About It), his final album for Apple Records.\n- \"Can't Stop Thinking About You\" is a love song in the style of a soul/R&B ballad.\n- George Harrison wrote \"Can't Stop Thinking About You\" toward the end of his marriage to Pattie Boyd.\n- George Harrison wrote \"Can't Stop Thinking About You\" while he was having an affair with Maureen Starkey, who was Ringo Starr's wife.\n- Maureen Starkey and Ringo Starr divorced in 1975.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
